  "definitions": [
    {
      "sense_number": 1,
      "gloss": "crash; fall; plunge",
      "explanation": "A sudden, uncontrolled fall from a height, typically used for aircraft crashes or falls from elevated places. Implies a dramatic, often catastrophic descent."
    }
  ],
  "examples": [
    {
      "id": "18763_tsuiraku_ex1",
      "japanese": "{飛行機|ひこうき}が{墜落|ついらく}した。",
      "english": "The airplane crashed.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "18763_tsuiraku_ex2",
      "japanese": "{墜落|ついらく}{事故|じこ}の{原因|げんいん}を{調査|ちょうさ}している。",
      "english": "They are investigating the cause of the crash.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "18763_tsuiraku_ex3",
      "japanese": "ヘリコプターが{山中|さんちゅう}に{墜落|ついらく}し、{乗員|じょういん}{全員|ぜんいん}が{救助|きゅうじょ}された。",
      "english": "A helicopter crashed in the mountains, and all crew members were rescued.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    }
  ],
  "notes": "Used with する to form the verb {墜落|ついらく}する (to crash, to plunge). Almost exclusively used for falls from significant heights, especially aircraft. Common collocations: {墜落|ついらく}{事故|じこ} (crash accident), {墜落|ついらく}{現場|げんば} (crash site), {墜落|ついらく}{防止|ぼうし} (fall prevention — in construction safety). Related: {落下|らっか} (falling — more general, includes dropping objects), {転落|てんらく} (fall — typically from an edge or ledge, e.g., a cliff or platform).",
